## QUIT
QUIT FORCE/S

Quit DeluxeMusic.
- FORCE -- Quit without asking to save unsaved changes

## NEW
NEW

Open a new blank score document.

## OPEN
OPEN FILENAME,FORCE/S

Open an existing score file.
- FILENAME -- Path to the score file (CMUS, DMCS, or MIDI format)
- FORCE -- Discard unsaved changes without asking

Example: OPEN "Work:Scores/MySong.CMUS"

## CLOSE
CLOSE FORCE/S

Close the current score.
- FORCE -- Close without asking to save

## SAVE
SAVE

Save the current score to its existing filename.

## SAVEAS
SAVEAS FILENAME,FORMAT/K,EMBEDSAMPLES/K,FORCE/S

Save the current score with options.
- FILENAME -- Destination path
- FORMAT -- File format: CMUS (default), DMCS, MIDI
- EMBEDSAMPLES -- YES or NO. Embed instrument samples in the file (for distribution)
- FORCE -- Overwrite without asking

Example: SAVEAS "Work:Scores/Song.CMUS" FORMAT CMUS EMBEDSAMPLES YES

## REVERT
REVERT FORCE/S

Revert to previously saved version of the score.
- FORCE -- Revert without confirmation

## PRINT
PRINT OPTIONS/S

Print the score.
- OPTIONS -- Open the Print As... dialog instead of printing directly

## UNDO
UNDO

Undo the last operation.

## COPY
COPY

Copy selected items to the clipboard.

## CUT
CUT

Cut selected items to the clipboard.

## PASTE
PASTE

Paste from clipboard into the score at the cursor position.

## PLAY
PLAY SECTION/S

Play the score.
- SECTION -- Play only the currently selected section (between section bars)

## STOP
STOP

Stop playback.

## RESUME
RESUME

Resume playback from where it was last stopped.

## CHANGEWINDOW
CHANGEWINDOW LEFT/N,TOP/N,WIDTH/N,HEIGHT/N

Move and resize the current window.
- LEFT -- X position in pixels
- TOP -- Y position in pixels
- WIDTH -- Width in pixels
- HEIGHT -- Height in pixels

## SIZEWINDOW
SIZEWINDOW WIDTH/N,HEIGHT/N

Resize the main document window.
- WIDTH -- New width in pixels
- HEIGHT -- New height in pixels

## WINDOW
WINDOW NAMES/M,OPEN/S,CLOSE/S,SNAPSHOT/S,ACTIVATE/S,MIN/S,MAX/S,FRONT/S,BACK/S,PREV/S,NEXT/S

Open, close, activate, or resize named command windows.
- NAMES -- Window name(s): TOOL, INSTRUMENT, PALETTE, TEMPO, etc.
- OPEN/CLOSE -- Open or close the window
- SNAPSHOT -- Save current position/size
- ACTIVATE -- Bring to front and make active
- MIN/MAX -- Minimize or maximize
- FRONT/BACK -- Move in front of or behind other windows
- PREV/NEXT -- Cycle through open document windows

Example: WINDOW TOOL OPEN
Example: WINDOW INSTRUMENT CLOSE

## MOVEWINDOW
MOVEWINDOW LEFT/N,TOP/N

Move a window to a new position.
- LEFT -- X position in pixels
- TOP -- Y position in pixels

## SCREENTOFRONT
SCREENTOFRONT

Move the DeluxeMusic screen to the front.

## SCREENTOBACK
SCREENTOBACK

Move the DeluxeMusic screen to the back.

## LOCKDISPLAY
LOCKDISPLAY

Inhibit screen refreshes. Use during batch ARexx operations for speed.
Always pair with UNLOCKDISPLAY.

## UNLOCKDISPLAY
UNLOCKDISPLAY

Re-enable screen refreshes after LOCKDISPLAY.

## UPDATEDISPLAY
UPDATEDISPLAY FORCE/S

Refresh the display.
- FORCE -- Force complete redraw

## LOCKGUI
LOCKGUI

Inhibit all keyboard and mouse input. Use during batch ARexx operations.
Always pair with UNLOCKGUI.

## UNLOCKGUI
UNLOCKGUI

Re-enable keyboard and mouse input after LOCKGUI.

## BEEPSCREEN
BEEPSCREEN

Beep or flash the screen.

## SETSTATUSBAR
SETSTATUSBAR TITLE

Place a message in the program's title bar.
- TITLE -- Text to display

Example: SETSTATUSBAR "Processing..."

## SAVESETTINGS
SAVESETTINGS

Save the GUI settings (window positions, macro assignments, etc.) to tooltypes.

## SETTOOL
SETTOOL TOOL/A

Select a tool in the tool window.
- TOOL -- Tool name: NOTE, REST, TIE, TEXT, DYNAMIC, TEMPO, CLEF, KEY, TIME, BAR, STAFF, BEAM, TUPLET, SLUR, CRESCENDO, DECRESCENDO, 8VA, 8VB, PEDAL, REHEARSAL

Example: SETTOOL NOTE

## SETACCIDENTAL
SETACCIDENTAL VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the accidental setting in the tool window.
- VALUE -- NATURAL, SHARP, FLAT, DOUBLESHARP, DOUBLEFLAT, NONE
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## SETDIVISION
SETDIVISION VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the note duration setting.
- VALUE -- WHOLE, HALF, QUARTER, EIGHTH, SIXTEENTH, THIRTYSECOND, SIXTYFOURTH
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

Example: SETDIVISION QUARTER

## SETDOT
SETDOT VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the dotted note setting.
- VALUE -- NONE, DOT, DOUBLEDOT
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## SETDYNAMIC
SETDYNAMIC VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the dynamics setting.
- VALUE -- Numeric value 0-127 (MIDI velocity), or PPP, PP, P, MP, MF, F, FF, FFF
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## SETTUPLET
SETTUPLET VALUE/A,UPDATE/S

Change the tuplet setting.
- VALUE -- NONE, TRIPLET, or a numeric ratio
- UPDATE -- Also update any currently selected notes

## REQUESTNOTIFY
REQUESTNOTIFY TITLE/K,PROMPT

Open a 1-button (OK) requester to display a message.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Message text

Example: REQUESTNOTIFY TITLE "Info" "Score has 42 measures"

## REQUESTRESPONSE
REQUESTRESPONSE TITLE/K,PROMPT,DEFAULT/K/N,BUTTONS/K

Open a 2-button requester for yes/no questions. Returns 1 or 0 in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Question text
- DEFAULT -- Default button (1=left, 0=right)
- BUTTONS -- Button labels separated by |

Example: REQUESTRESPONSE TITLE "Confirm" "Transpose all?" BUTTONS "Yes|No"

## REQUESTNUM
REQUESTNUM TITLE/K,PROMPT,DEFAULT/K/N,BUTTONS/K

Prompt the user for a number. Returns the number in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Prompt text
- DEFAULT -- Default value
- BUTTONS -- Button labels

## REQUESTSTRING
REQUESTSTRING TITLE/K,PROMPT,DEFAULT/K,BUTTONS/K

Prompt the user for a string. Returns the string in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Window title
- PROMPT -- Prompt text
- DEFAULT -- Default string value
- BUTTONS -- Button labels

## REQUESTFILE
REQUESTFILE TITLE/K,PATH/K,FILE/K,PATTERN/K

Prompt the user for a filename. Returns the full path in RESULT.
- TITLE -- Requester title
- PATH -- Initial directory
- FILE -- Initial filename
- PATTERN -- AmigaDOS pattern filter (e.g. #?.CMUS)

Example: REQUESTFILE TITLE "Open Score" PATH "Work:Scores" PATTERN "#?.CMUS"

## GOTO
GOTO TRACK/K/N,STAFF/K/N,MEASURE/K/N,CHORD/K/N,CLOCK/K/N,HIDDEN/S

Move the cursor to a specified location.
- TRACK -- Track number (1-based)
- STAFF -- Staff number within track (1-based)
- MEASURE -- Measure number (1-based)
- CHORD -- Chord position within measure
- CLOCK -- Clock tick position within measure
- HIDDEN -- Allow moving to hidden items

Example: GOTO MEASURE 5 STAFF 1
Example: GOTO TRACK 2 MEASURE 1

## POSITION
POSITION SOF/S,EOF/S,SOM/S,EOM/S,HIDDEN/S

Move cursor to a boundary position.
- SOF -- Start of file (first item in score)
- EOF -- End of file (last item in score)
- SOM -- Start of current measure
- EOM -- End of current measure
- HIDDEN -- Allow positioning at hidden items

Example: POSITION SOF

## NEXT
NEXT EVENT/S,NOTE/S,INTERVAL/S,CHORD/S,MEASURE/S,STAFF/S,TRACK/S,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,COUNT/N

Move cursor to the next item.
- EVENT -- Next event of any type
- NOTE -- Next note
- INTERVAL -- Next interval/note within a chord
- CHORD -- Next chord position
- MEASURE -- Next measure
- STAFF -- Next staff
- TRACK -- Next track
- SELECTED -- Move to next selected (1) or unselected (0) item
- HIDDEN -- Include hidden items
- COUNT -- Number of steps to move

Example: NEXT NOTE
Example: NEXT MEASURE COUNT 4

## PREVIOUS
PREVIOUS EVENT/S,NOTE/S,INTERVAL/S,CHORD/S,MEASURE/S,STAFF/S,TRACK/S,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,COUNT/N

Move cursor to the previous item. Same parameters as NEXT.

Example: PREVIOUS MEASURE

## SELECTITEM
SELECTITEM ADD/S,REMOVE/S,TOGGLE/S

Select the item after the cursor.
- ADD -- Add to current selection (don't deselect others)
- REMOVE -- Remove from selection
- TOGGLE -- Toggle selection state

## SELECTALL
SELECTALL

Select all items in the score.

## DESELECTALL
DESELECTALL

Deselect all selected items.

## INSERTITEM
INSERTITEM TYPE,TRACK/K/N,DURATION/K,CLOCKS/K/N,DOTS/K/N,TUPLET/K/N,ACCIDENTAL/K,OCTAVE/K/N,LINE/K/N,PITCH/K/N,LETTER/K,NOTESTEM/K,LOUDNESS/K/N,FONT/K,RATE/K/N,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,NOFIX/S

Add an item to the score at the cursor position.
- TYPE -- Item type: NOTE, REST, BAR, TEXT, DYNAMIC, TEMPO, CLEF, KEY, TIME, REHEARSAL
- TRACK -- Target track number
- DURATION -- WHOLE, HALF, QUARTER, EIGHTH, SIXTEENTH, THIRTYSECOND, SIXTYFOURTH
- CLOCKS -- Duration in clock ticks (alternative to DURATION)
- DOTS -- Number of dots (0, 1, or 2)
- TUPLET -- Tuplet ratio (e.g. 3 for triplet)
- ACCIDENTAL -- NATURAL, SHARP, FLAT, DOUBLESHARP, DOUBLEFLAT, NONE
- OCTAVE -- Octave number (0-9, middle C = octave 4)
- LINE -- Staff line position
- PITCH -- MIDI pitch number (0-127, middle C = 60)
- LETTER -- Note letter: C, D, E, F, G, A, B
- NOTESTEM -- UP, DOWN, or AUTO
- LOUDNESS -- MIDI velocity (0-127)
- FONT -- Text font name (for TEXT type)
- RATE -- Tempo in BPM (for TEMPO type)
- SELECTED -- 1 to create as selected
- HIDDEN -- Create as hidden item
- NOFIX -- Disable re-sorting (use with RESORTEVENTS for batch operations)

Example: INSERTITEM NOTE LETTER C OCTAVE 4 DURATION QUARTER
Example: INSERTITEM REST DURATION HALF
Example: INSERTITEM TEMPO RATE 120

## INSERTMEASURE
INSERTMEASURE

Add a new empty measure after the current measure.

## CLEAR
CLEAR FORCE/S

Delete all data from the score.
- FORCE -- Clear without confirmation

## ERASE
ERASE

Delete all currently selected items.

## CLEARMOD
CLEARMOD

Remove all accidentals and tuplets from selected items.

## DELBACKWD
DELBACKWD

Delete the item before the cursor.

## DELFWD
DELFWD

Delete the item after the cursor.

## DELETEMEASURE
DELETEMEASURE COUNT/N

Delete measure(s) starting from the current measure.
- COUNT -- Number of measures to delete (default: 1)

## CHANGEITEM
CHANGEITEM TYPE,TRACK/K/N,DURATION/K,CLOCKS/K/N,DOTS/K/N,TUPLET/K/N,ACCIDENTAL/K,OCTAVE/K/N,LINE/K/N,PITCH/K/N,LETTER/K,NOTESTEM/K,LOUDNESS/K/N,FONT/K,RATE/K/N,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,NOFIX/S

Modify the item after the cursor. Same parameters as INSERTITEM.
Only specified parameters are changed; others remain as they are.
- NOFIX -- Disable re-sorting during batch edits (use with RESORTEVENTS)

Example: CHANGEITEM DURATION HALF
Example: CHANGEITEM LETTER D OCTAVE 5

## CHANGESELECTED
CHANGESELECTED TYPE,TRACK/K/N,DURATION/K,CLOCKS/K/N,DOTS/K/N,TUPLET/K/N,ACCIDENTAL/K,OCTAVE/K/N,LINE/K/N,PITCH/K/N,LETTER/K,NOTESTEM/K,LOUDNESS/K/N,FONT/K,RATE/K/N,SELECTED/N,HIDDEN/S,NOFIX/S

Modify all currently selected items. Same parameters as CHANGEITEM.

Example: CHANGESELECTED LOUDNESS 100

## CHANGETONE
CHANGETONE HALFSTEP/K/N,LEVEL/K/N,OCTAVE/K/N

Change the pitch of selected notes.
- HALFSTEP -- Transpose by N half steps (positive=up, negative=down)
- LEVEL -- Transpose by N staff levels (diatonic steps)
- OCTAVE -- Transpose by N octaves

Example: CHANGETONE HALFSTEP 7 (transpose up a fifth)
Example: CHANGETONE OCTAVE -1 (transpose down one octave)

## FLIPNOTESTEM
FLIPNOTESTEM DIRECTION

Flip the direction of selected note stems.
- DIRECTION -- UP, DOWN, or AUTO

## GROUPITEM
GROUPITEM ACTION/A,TYPE/A,DIRECTION

Add or remove grouping (ties, beams, 8va's, etc.)
- ACTION -- ADD or REMOVE
- TYPE -- TIE, BEAM, SLUR, 8VA, 8VB, CRESCENDO, DECRESCENDO, PEDAL
- DIRECTION -- OPEN or CLOSE (start or end of the group)

Example: GROUPITEM ADD TIE OPEN (start a tie)
Example: GROUPITEM ADD TIE CLOSE (end the tie)
Example: GROUPITEM ADD BEAM OPEN (start a beam group)

## DOUBLETIME
DOUBLETIME

Double the duration of all selected notes (e.g. quarter -> half).

## HALFTIME
HALFTIME

Halve the duration of all selected notes (e.g. quarter -> eighth).

## JOINMEASURE
JOINMEASURE

Join the current measure with the next measure into one.

## SPLITMEASURE
SPLITMEASURE

Split the current measure into two at the cursor position.

## REALIGNMEASURE
REALIGNMEASURE

Realign note spacing in the current measure.

## SETBARATTR
SETBARATTR BEGINSECTION/S,ENDSECTION/S,ENDING1/K,ENDING2/K,BEGINREPEAT/K,ENDREPEAT/K,DOUBLEBAR/K

Change bar line attributes for the current measure.
- BEGINSECTION/ENDSECTION -- Mark section boundaries
- ENDING1 -- First ending bracket: OPEN, CLOSE, or NONE
- ENDING2 -- Second ending bracket: OPEN, CLOSE, or NONE
- BEGINREPEAT -- Begin repeat: YES or NO
- ENDREPEAT -- End repeat: YES or NO
- DOUBLEBAR -- Double bar line: YES or NO

Example: SETBARATTR BEGINREPEAT YES
Example: SETBARATTR ENDING1 OPEN

## SETCLEF
SETCLEF TYPE/A,STAFF/N/A,START/N,END/N

Change the clef for a staff.
- TYPE -- TREBLE, BASS, ALTO, TENOR, PERCUSSION
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- START -- Starting measure number
- END -- Ending measure number

Example: SETCLEF TREBLE 1 1 999

## SETKEYSIGNATURE
SETKEYSIGNATURE TYPE/A,STAFF/N/A,START/N,END/N,TRANSPOSE/K

Change the key signature.
- TYPE -- Key name: C, G, D, A, E, B, F#, C#, F, Bb, Eb, Ab, Db, Gb, Cb, Am, Em, Bm, F#m, C#m, G#m, D#m, A#m, Dm, Gm, Cm, Fm, Bbm, Ebm, Abm
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- START -- Starting measure
- END -- Ending measure
- TRANSPOSE -- YES or NO. Transpose existing notes to match new key

Example: SETKEYSIGNATURE G 1 1 999
Example: SETKEYSIGNATURE Bb 1 5 999 TRANSPOSE YES

## SETTIMESIGNATURE
SETTIMESIGNATURE BEATS/N/A,DURATION/N/A,MEASURE/N

Change the time signature.
- BEATS -- Number of beats per measure
- DURATION -- Beat duration (4=quarter, 8=eighth, 2=half, etc.)
- MEASURE -- Starting measure number (default: current measure)

Example: SETTIMESIGNATURE 3 4 (3/4 time)
Example: SETTIMESIGNATURE 6 8 1 (6/8 from measure 1)

## SETSTAFF
SETSTAFF STAFF/N/A,ATTR/A,VALUE/A

Change staff attributes.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- ATTR -- Attribute name: NAME, CHANNEL, INSTRUMENT, TRANSPOSE, VOLUME, PAN, VISIBLE
- VALUE -- New value for the attribute

Example: SETSTAFF 1 NAME "Piano"
Example: SETSTAFF 2 CHANNEL 2
Example: SETSTAFF 1 VISIBLE YES

## GETATTR
GETATTR OBJECT/A,NAME,FIELD

Get information about DeluxeMusic's status. Returns value in RESULT.
- OBJECT -- Object type: APPLICATION, DOCUMENT, SCORE, WINDOW
- NAME -- Object name (if applicable)
- FIELD -- Specific field to query: FILENAME, MODIFIED, TRACKS, STAVES, MEASURES, etc.

Example: GETATTR DOCUMENT "" FILENAME
Example: GETATTR SCORE "" MEASURES

## GETERRORINFO
GETERRORINFO ERROR/N/A

Get a text description of an error number. Returns description in RESULT.
- ERROR -- Error number to look up

## GETPOSITION
GETPOSITION FIELD

Get current cursor position. Returns value in RESULT.
- FIELD -- TRACK, STAFF, MEASURE, CHORD, CLOCK, EVENT

Example: GETPOSITION MEASURE

## GETITEMATTR
GETITEMATTR FIELD

Get information about the item at/after the cursor. Returns value in RESULT.
- FIELD -- TYPE, DURATION, CLOCKS, DOTS, TUPLET, ACCIDENTAL, OCTAVE, LINE, PITCH, LETTER, NOTESTEM, LOUDNESS, FONT, RATE, SELECTED, HIDDEN

Example: GETITEMATTR TYPE
Example: GETITEMATTR PITCH

## GETCLEF
GETCLEF STAFF/N/A,MEASURE/N,EFFECTIVE/S

Get clef information. Returns clef type in RESULT.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- MEASURE -- Measure number (default: current)
- EFFECTIVE -- Return the clef in effect at that point (may be set in an earlier measure)

## GETKEYSIGNATURE
GETKEYSIGNATURE STAFF/N/A,MEASURE/N,EFFECTIVE/S

Get key signature. Returns key name in RESULT.
- STAFF -- Staff number
- MEASURE -- Measure number
- EFFECTIVE -- Return the key in effect at that point

## GETSTAFF
GETSTAFF STAFF/N/A,ATTR/A

Get staff attribute value. Returns value in RESULT.
- STAFF -- Staff number (1-based)
- ATTR -- Attribute: NAME, CHANNEL, INSTRUMENT, TRANSPOSE, VOLUME, PAN, VISIBLE

Example: GETSTAFF 1 NAME

## GETTIMESIGNATURE
GETTIMESIGNATURE MEASURE/N,EFFECTIVE/S

Get time signature. Returns "beats/duration" in RESULT (e.g. "4/4").
- MEASURE -- Measure number
- EFFECTIVE -- Return the time signature in effect at that point

## RESORTEVENTS
RESORTEVENTS

Re-sort all events after batch editing with NOFIX.
Recommended batch editing pattern:
1. LOCKGUI
2. LOCKDISPLAY
3. Edit items with NOFIX flag
4. RESORTEVENTS
5. UNLOCKDISPLAY
6. UNLOCKGUI

## RX
RX CONSOLE/S,ASYNC/S,COMMAND/F

Execute an ARexx script file.
- CONSOLE -- Open a console window for the script
- ASYNC -- Run asynchronously (don't wait for completion)
- COMMAND -- Script filename and arguments (rest of line)

Example: RX "Rexx:Transpose.rexx"

## RXS
RXS CONSOLE/S,ASYNC/S,COMMAND/F

Execute an ARexx command string directly.
- CONSOLE -- Open a console window
- ASYNC -- Run asynchronously
- COMMAND -- ARexx code to execute (rest of line)

Example: RXS "say 'Hello from DMusic'"

## ABORTSCRIPTS
ABORTSCRIPTS

Abort all currently executing ARexx scripts.

## CMDSHELL
CMDSHELL

Open the interactive ARexx command shell window.

## HELP
HELP COMMAND

Display usage information for an ARexx command. Returns help text in RESULT.
- COMMAND -- Command name to get help for (omit for list of all commands)

Example: HELP INSERTITEM

## LEARN
LEARN FILE/K,STOP/S

Start or stop recording a macro.
- FILE -- Save macro to this file
- STOP -- Stop recording

Example: LEARN FILE "Rexx:MyMacro.rexx" (start recording)
Example: LEARN STOP (stop recording)

## PLAYMACRO
PLAYMACRO

Execute the last recorded macro.

## SAVEMACRO
SAVEMACRO FILE/K

Save the last recorded macro to a file.
- FILE -- Destination filename

Example: SAVEMACRO FILE "Rexx:MyMacro.rexx"
